{
  "summary": "Enables the `-Wmissing-noreturn` compiler warning flag in CMake and annotates non-returning functions, methods, and lambdas with `[[noreturn]]`. Because it is based on #36087, it also introduces `AssertUnreachable()`, replaces falsy assertions like `assert(false)` across the tree via scripted diff, and adds a linter enforcing this. Additionally, it qualifies bare C `abort()` and `exit()` calls with `std::`.",
  "problem": "Functions that never return without `[[noreturn]]` annotations cause compiler static analysis false positives, such as spurious `-Wreturn-type` warnings. Without automated compiler warning enforcement via `-Wmissing-noreturn`, missing annotations regularly recur. Unreachable branches using `assert(false)` can also be compiled out in non-debug builds rather than reliably terminating execution and informing the compiler's control flow analysis.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description cites compiler diagnostics: \"Missing `[[noreturn]]` attributes can cause compiler false positives and other issues; see discussion in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35896#discussion_r3726612556.\""
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#36087"
    ],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "A significant portion of the diff consists of mechanical changes replacing `assert(false)` with `AssertUnreachable()` across nearly 100 files, implemented via a verification script.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased or updated slightly, preserving the commit structure and scope.",
  "card": "Enables the -Wmissing-noreturn compiler warning in CMake and marks functions, methods, and lambdas that unconditionally throw or abort with [[noreturn]]. Based on PR 36087, it also introduces AssertUnreachable() to replace assert(false) across the codebase and adds a linter forbidding falsy assertions. This prevents compiler static analysis false positives such as spurious missing-return warnings.",
